    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne054\tJonah proposed restoring one moment of hesitation and adding a short scene earlier that shows the participant's obligations in the town.\ne055\tHe would keep the final sequence.\ne056\tI can imagine that working.\ne057\tBut he also wants the credit to read “A film by Jonah Vale and Mira Chen,” even though it is audio, because the showcase uses that language.\ne058\tI want “Reported by Mira Chen, sound and story by Jonah Vale.”\ne059\tHe hears my version as splitting the work into journalism and art.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne060\tHis edit proposal sounds like a substantive attempt to preserve uncertainty without dissolving the ending, though you should judge it in the cut rather than in description.\ne061\tThe credit disagreement is not merely wording; each version tells a story about what the work is.\ne062\tEqual top-line authorship plus a second line naming reporting, editing, and sound may acknowledge collaboration and labor, but only if neither of you experiences the top line as erasing the actual imbalance you are trying to name.\n[Turn 7 USER]\ne063\tMy provisional plan is to hear Jonah's revised cut before deciding about postponement.\ne064\tI will compare it with the approved version and write down the exact interpretive difference I still see, if any.\ne065\tFor credit, I will propose equal top-line authorship with detailed role credits below, but I am not sure I can accept that if he still treats structural decisions as his domain.\ne066\tI want to separate the current film from the rules for our next collaboration, and I am not sure they can really be separated.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne067\tListening before deciding prevents an abstract disagreement from hardening around a cut that does not yet exist.\ne068\tYour uncertainty about credit and future authority is also legitimate: a current credit can acknowledge completed work, while the feelings behind it may still determine whether you collaborate again.\ne069\tYou do not need to solve the next project before the showcase, but you may need to avoid using a harmonious credit line as evidence that the underlying process felt mutual.\ne070\tThe revised cut could resolve the edit question and leave the partnership question open.",
